course: dictionary
lesson: 8681
title: Seek: look for, or try to get
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Seek is a short word with a big job. It means to look for something or someone, as in «hide-and-seek», where one player goes looking for the others. It can also mean to try to get something you need, like help, advice or safety.
explain: The words around seek give you clues. In the story of the girl in the dryer, the door shut and she could not open it, and «her mum heard her knocking». Someone was looking for her, and help came. When you are in danger, you seek help from a trusted adult.
explain: Try the sentence check. Put look for or try to get in place of seek and see if it still makes sense. «Seek shelter» from the rain means try to get shelter from the rain, so the check works.
fact: Seek means to look for something or someone. It can also mean to try to get something, such as help, advice or shelter.
fact: In hide-and-seek, the seeker looks for the players who are hiding.
fact: In safety lessons, «seek help» means go to a trusted adult, such as a teacher or a parent.
fact: Seek is a verb with four forms: seek, seeks, sought, seeking. «Sought» is the past form, as in «She sought advice from her teacher.»
fact: Many countries have their own version of hide-and-seek. In Chinese it is called zhuō mícáng.
exercise: In hide-and-seek, what does the seeker do? | Counts the cards in a deck | Taps the wall and runs away | *Looks for the players who are hiding | Hides in the hedge for an hour
exercise: «Lost children should seek help from a trusted adult.» Find and copy one word that means look for or try to get. | trusted | adult | Lost | *seek
exercise: Sam says seek means to sit still and wait. Is Sam right? | Yes, seek means to sleep | No, seek means to shout | *No, seek means to look for something or to try to get it | Yes, seek means to sit still and wait
test: «He sought advice from his coach before the match.» What does sought mean here? | Forgot | *Asked for, looked for | Hid from | Gave away
test: Which is the best way to seek help if you feel unsafe? | Walk home alone in the dark | *Tell a trusted adult, such as a teacher or a parent | Keep it secret forever | Hide under the bed and wait
exam: In «seek shelter» from the rain, what does seek mean? | *To look for and try to get something | To run very fast | To sing loudly | To go to sleep
